Subject: sros2: pass an EllipticCurve instance to generate_private_key
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ros2/sros2/commit/0bc98988baa76c8793bc728c57a30cfa19edd2ae
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/ros2/sros2.git 80a08ffa1bccd2de602c2acd120b209ad5f8ce83
Verify: test tests/ros_test.go::TestROSAPK

sros2 passes the ec.SECP256R1 class where cryptography expects an EllipticCurve instance. cryptography 43 only warns
(CryptographyDeprecationWarning), and cryptography 47 raises "TypeError: curve must be an EllipticCurve instance", so
create_keystore and create_enclave fail on the alpine leaf. Passing ec.SECP256R1() works on both and stops the warning
on debian.

--- a/sros2/sros2/_utilities.py
+++ b/sros2/sros2/_utilities.py
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@ def build_key_and_cert(subject_name, *, ca=False, ca_key=None, issuer_name=''):
         issuer_name = subject_name
 
     # DDS-Security section 9.3.1 calls for prime256v1, for which SECP256R1 is an alias
-    private_key = ec.generate_private_key(ec.SECP256R1, cryptography_backend())
+    private_key = ec.generate_private_key(ec.SECP256R1(), cryptography_backend())
     if not ca_key:
         ca_key = private_key
 
